<item>
<title>Telegram macOS</title>
<description>New:&lt;br&gt;• Hidden chats: set a phrase in Settings &gt; Privacy and Security &gt; Hidden Chats, then type it in chat search to open the chats you hide there. Everywhere else they stay out of sight, including the chat list, search, notifications, badges and calls&lt;br&gt;• Each phrase opens its own set of hidden chats. Leave with ⌘L or the Leave button; hidden chats also close on sleep, screen lock or after five idle minutes&lt;br&gt;• Hidden chats are a Mac-only feature: phrases and hidden chats stay in this app on this Mac and don't sync, so your other devices keep showing these chats as usual&lt;br&gt;• Don't forget your phrase: it isn't stored anywhere and can't be recovered. Without it, those chats stay hidden on this Mac until you log out of Telegram here and log back in&lt;br&gt;• Dictator's remote control bot works in groups: /ask, /tldr and /draft answer only you, with buttons to send the answer to the chat or save it in the bot chat&lt;br&gt;• Ask Dictator inline in any chat with @yourbot followed by a question; answers that would reveal anything private go to the bot chat instead&lt;br&gt;• The bot paired with Dictator appears first when you type @ in a message&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• The chat moves smoothly when a bot's keyboard appears, changes or closes&lt;br&gt;• The Global Search prompt for posts is centered and its button is a Liquid Glass capsule&lt;br&gt;• Updated to the latest Telegram core, including the new on-chain gift sales and offers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;• Opening an unjoined channel could clear its messages behind a spinner a few seconds after they appeared&lt;br&gt;• The Optimizing Database screen and other early startup screens now appear in your language&lt;br&gt;</description>
<pubDate>2026-17-11 23:09:08</pubDate>
